        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0328" n="256" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg256"/>

                <head>No. 39.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West
                        to Earl Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 13, 1882</date>.
                        (Received April 3.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have honor to inclose to your
                    lordship herewith copies of resolutions respecting the protection of American
                    citizens abroad, which were introduced for reference to the Committee on Foreign
                    Relations by Mr. Crapo, Representative from Massachusetts.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE WEST.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d164-a1.xml" xpointer="d164-a1"/>
            </div>
